WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:11.795
What if you want to invest in dozens of top companies across India or the world, but you don't have the time or money to research and buy 50 individual stocks?

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:20.365
This is where an ETF, or Exchange-Traded Fund, becomes a powerful tool for modern investors.

00:00:20.365 --> 00:00:36.068
An ETF is an investment fund that holds a diversified basket of securities—such as stocks, bonds, or commodities—and trades on a public stock exchange just like an individual stock.

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:52.904
For example, an ETF tracking the NIFTY 50 index holds shares in 50 of India's largest and most established corporations across banking, information technology, consumer goods, energy, and healthcare.

00:00:52.904 --> 00:00:57.682
Imagine trying to buy all 50 NIFTY companies individually.

00:00:57.682 --> 00:01:06.706
You would need tens of thousands of rupees, pay multiple brokerage fees, and spend hours balancing your portfolio.

00:01:06.706 --> 00:01:15.313
With a NIFTY 50 ETF, you can buy a single unit for just ₹250 to ₹300.

00:01:15.313 --> 00:01:26.094
In one single trade, your money is automatically spread across giants like Reliance, TCS, HDFC Bank, and Infosys.

00:01:26.094 --> 00:01:29.688
ETFs provide three major benefits:

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:40.768
First, instant diversification: if one company has an unexpected decline, the other 49 companies cushion your overall portfolio.

00:01:40.768 --> 00:01:50.794
Second, real-time liquidity: you can buy and sell ETF units at prevailing market prices anytime during market trading hours.

00:01:50.794 --> 00:02:08.893
Third, ultra-low cost: because most index ETFs passively track an index without active fund manager salaries, their expense ratios are often as low as 0.05% to 0.20% per year.

00:02:08.893 --> 00:02:15.716
Beginners often assume that because ETFs are diversified, they cannot lose money.

00:02:15.716 --> 00:02:17.786
That is incorrect.

00:02:17.786 --> 00:02:28.685
An ETF eliminates single-company failure risk, but it still reflects broader market downturns when the overall economy experiences volatility.

00:02:28.685 --> 00:02:37.292
Keep in mind that ETFs can have minor tracking errors and bid-ask spreads during volatile market sessions.

00:02:37.292 --> 00:02:47.135
An ETF gives you a diversified basket of top companies in a single, low-cost, transparent trade on the stock exchange.
